      "type": "core.input.comment",
      "name": "comment",
      "x": 107.7,
      "y": 72.5,
      "text": "The timeline and beatline modules can be used to arrange different kinds of information very precisely in time. A timeLine uses seconds for its horizontal axis. A beatLine uses beats and subdivisions of beat. Other than that they are very similar.\n\n A timeLine is somewhat like the multi-track recorder that is common in other music programs. The difference here is that it is a module that can be connected to other modules. Also, you can have multiple timeLines in a single piece. One timeLine can trigger another timeLine. and a timeLine can even contain a patch that contains other timeLines. So they are very flexible.",
      "w": 533.7124,
      "h": 227.11084
    }
  ],
